# Destination: .npmrc at the root of nfc-development
#
# TEMPORARY. Delete this file in the pull request that removes src/mobile from the
# workspaces array (PR 11).
#
# Why it exists. npm install on a clean checkout of this repository fails with ERESOLVE,
# exit 1, verified twice during the August 2026 audit:
#
#   peer react@"^16.8" from @react-native-community/async-storage@1.12.1
#   against react@18.3.1
#
# The conflict is entirely inside src/mobile, a workspace that is out of scope, does not
# build, and has no native projects. Because npm installs workspaces together, that
# conflict blocks the install for the web app and the API as well.
#
# Two ways to unblock it. Removing src/mobile from workspaces is the right one and it
# needs Dan's agreement, so it cannot gate the lockfile. This file is the other one: it
# makes the install deterministic today, in the repository, visibly, rather than living in
# a command line flag that every developer and every CI job has to remember and that no
# document mentions. The audit found the flag was needed and that neither README.md nor
# CONTRIBUTING.md says so.
#
# The cost of this file is that peer dependency conflicts are not reported at install
# time. That is acceptable for exactly as long as the only conflict is a deprecated
# package in a workspace nobody builds, and not one day longer, which is why its deletion
# is written into PR 11 rather than left to memory.
legacy-peer-deps=true
